Ladybird sizes unbreakable text tokens from their glyph ink. Blink
calls ComputeInkMetrics() from MathTokenLayoutAlgorithm::Layout().
For a math-variant glyph, WebKit measures the bounds in its
RenderMathMLToken::firstLineBaseline() and layoutBlock() methods. Gecko
reads ink in nsMathMLTokenFrame::Place() and also uses the font metrics.

With STIX Two Math at 40px, the engines disagree on the height of
a dotted x with accent set to false. Ladybird follows Chrome for
the accent gap: both leave 7px between the letter and the dot.
Their total heights are 32.45px in Ladybird and 31.80px in Chrome
158.0.8127.37. The same expression is 44.32px tall in Firefox 151.0 and
48.11px in WebKit 26.5.
